    "text_delta": "y application and interview performance would be very valuable for my professional development.\"*\n\n#### C. Consult a Confidential Campus Resource\nBefore raising concerns formally or publicly, consult:\n* **The University Ombudsperson:** An ombudsperson can offer confidential, informal guidance on university procedures and whether the search complied with internal rules.\n* **The Faculty Union / Academic Staff Association:** If you or colleagues belong to the academic union, their representatives are often very familiar with whether this department has a history of procedural hiring irregularities.\n\n#### D. Decide Whether to Raise Panel Composition\n* **If there was a policy violation:** You can raise this procedurally with the university’s HR/Equity office (e.g., *\"I noticed the panel did not reflect the university’s diversity requirements outlined in Section X of the recruitment policy\"*).\n* **If policies were followed (or guidelines were vague):** Pointing solely to the panel's gender composition without documented procedural breaches or written feedback is unlikely to change the outcome and could result in administrative pushback. It is usually best to secure written feedback first before deciding whether formal grievance or complaint is appropriate.\n",
